+### 4.6 A worked white-dwarf charge: retarded scattering memory and its orbital-timescale collapse
+
+**Imported from prior work.** The inner white dwarf of PSR J0337+1715 has timing mass 0.1975 \(M_\odot\) and spectroscopic \(T_{\rm eff}=15{,}800\pm100\) K, \(\log g=5.82\pm0.05\) and \(R=0.091\pm0.005\,R_\odot\) \cite{kaplan2014j0337}. The orbital elements follow \cite{ransom2014triple,archibald2018universality,voisin2020sep}.
+
+**Counterexample candidate.** We asked whether the smallest internal state of this carrier, the displacement of its own matter, can be the lag-responding state of Section 3. The declared theory has one massless scalar with \(A(\varphi)=e^{\beta\varphi^2/2}\), \(\beta=-4\), \(\alpha=\beta\varphi\), and linearization point \(\varphi_\infty=10^{-3}\). The background is a static, weak-field, hot helium-core model with \(M=0.198\,M_\odot\), \(R=6.91\times10^9\) cm, \(T_{\rm eff}=15{,}898\) K, \(\log g=5.740\) and a gray Eddington envelope built with Rosseland tables. An ingoing C\(^3\) pulse \(U=\eta r_0 g((t+x/c)/D)\), \(g(s)=(4s(1-s))^4\), \(D=1.717\) ms, \(\eta=10^{-30}\), drives the coupled evolution of baryons, gas, photon transport and the returned GR metric until \(T=2D\). The compact charge is \(q=-U_{\rm out}/M\), so the exterior monopole is \(\delta\varphi\to-qGM/(c^2r)\). Interior refinement by 1, 2 and 4, followed by mass normalization, gives
+
+\begin{equation}
+q(T)=-2.335\times10^{-51},\qquad \frac{q}{\eta\varphi_\infty^2}=-2.335\times10^{-15},
+\label{eq:wd-charge}
+\end{equation}
+
+with observed order 2.00 and a 2x-to-4x change of \(-1.2\%\).
+
+**Counterexample candidate.** The charge is a dynamical response. The instantaneous product of the pulse and the background geometry contributes \(10^{-8}\) of it, while the rest-mass redistribution of baryons contributes 0.999996. The redistribution conserves mass, and 99.9% of the endpoint charge comes from layers that the pulse has already left. Disabling the Planck–Larkin occupation probabilities in the equation of state and opacities changes the charge by at most \(2.2\times10^{-10}\).
+
+**Proven.** For pressureless matter at linear order, the radial displacement
+
+\begin{equation}
+\xi=4c^2\frac{a^2}{B^2}\eta R_dD^2\Big[\Big(\frac{\varphi_0'}{r}-\frac{\varphi_0}{r^2}\Big)F_2(p)+\frac{\varphi_0x'}{rcD}F_1(p)\Big],\qquad p=\frac{t+x/c}{D},
+\label{eq:free-fall}
+\end{equation}
+
+with \(F_1=\int_0^pg\) and \(F_2=\int_0^pF_1\), solves \(\ddot\xi=-c^2(a^2/B^2)\partial_r[\alpha(\varphi_0)\delta\varphi]\) exactly (the symbolic residual is zero). Passing the resulting face mass fluxes \(4\pi r^2B\rho_0\xi\) through the same retarded propagator reproduces the continuum limit of the coupled chain to \(5.2\times10^{-5}\).
+
+**Counterexample candidate.** The charge is linear in the face densities, and its kernel is nearly single-signed: a relative density change of 0.9988 in the maximum norm is needed to reverse the sign. The kernel centroid lies 363 km below the surface, at gray optical depth 1.06, so the charge-carrying layers form the photosphere.
+
+**Counterexample candidate.** The endpoint value is not a static charge. The static-window monopole of the displaced configuration is \(3.6\times10^{-54}\), which is 1/640 of it. The remainder is the part of the retarded monopole, \(q(u)=M^{-1}\sum_e w_e\,(c/2r_e)\int_{u-r_e/c}^{u+r_e/c}\delta M_e\,dt\) with \(w=\alpha(\varphi_0)a\), that has not yet cancelled inside the light-crossing window. We checked this with a whole-star linear adiabatic radial model with Newtonian self-gravity, driven by the same force and by the regular pulse reflected through the centre. The model reproduces the endpoint charge to \(-0.81\%\) and the free-fall displacement to \(1.2\times10^{-6}\). Over the full history:
+
+- While the pulse moves inward (to 0.35 s), the charge stays negative and grows by about twelve orders of magnitude, reaching \(-7.5\times10^{-41}\) when the pulse arrives at the centre.
+- On the outgoing pass, the signal accumulates along the pulse's own light cone and oscillates in sign. Its largest value, \(3.5\times10^{-36}\) (\(1.5\times10^{-11}\) of the incident amplitude), occurs at exit.
+- After the pulse has left, the star rings in its radial p modes, with dominant periods of 44–59 s and an amplitude of order \(10^{-44}\).
+
+**Proven.** Because the radial stiffness is positive definite (\(\omega_0^2=1.25\times10^{-3}\) s\(^{-2}\)), the post-pulse charge is a finite sum of nonzero-frequency modes, and its time average vanishes. For positive mode damping it tends to zero. The permanent charge is therefore zero at first order in \(\eta\).
+
+**Proven.** The corrections to the endpoint value are small:
+
+- The self-consistent GR fixed point differs from the once-returned solution by at most \(2\pi G\rho_{\max}T^2=4.5\times10^{-18}\), from radial self-gravity feedback.
+- Outside a spherical source in flat space, \(U=r\,\delta\varphi\) depends only on the retarded time, so the readout radius already gives the value at infinity. The curvature tail is at most \(M/r_{\rm out}=4.2\times10^{-6}\) (Conjectural).
+- Because \(\alpha=\beta\varphi\) is exactly linear, the second-order force and source terms are \(|\delta\varphi|/\varphi_0=1.0\times10^{-27}\) of the first-order ones.
+- Invariance under \(\varphi\to-\varphi\) makes \(q/\eta\) even in \(\varphi_\infty\). The readout weight is \(\alpha(\varphi_0)/r\), so the dynamical part scales as \(\varphi_\infty^2\) (Conjectural for the \(10^{-8}\) direct part).
+- ADM normalization changes the value by \(6.8\times10^{-11}\) (Conjectural).
+
+**Counterexample candidate.** For the observed photosphere we integrated a spherical gray Eddington envelope with the declared equation of state and Rosseland tables, at fixed mass. It reproduces the declared background to 0.25% in the charge layers. At the observed \(\log g\) and \(T_{\rm eff}\) it multiplies the endpoint charge by 3.2 (1\(\sigma\): 1.6–6.2; 2\(\sigma\): 0.78–11.2). A converged non-gray LTE radiative equilibrium with H and He continuum opacities (flux constancy \(5.5\times10^{-5}\), surface temperature \(0.64\,T_{\rm eff}\)) multiplies it by a further 2.1, to 6.9 (1\(\sigma\): 3.9–11.7). The sign is unchanged in every case.
+
+**Conjectural.** At orbital timescales the memory collapses to static coefficients in every channel we examined.
+
+- Radial. The lowest radial adiabatic mode has period 178 s. A drive longer than the star exerts a monopole force \(3.3\times10^{-8}\) times that of the pulse, and \((\omega/\omega_0)^2=1.6\times10^{-6}\) at the inner orbit.
+- Tidal. Linear response couples the monopole charge only to the \(l=0\) part of the drive (Proven). The apsidal constant is \(k_2=3.3\times10^{-4}\), and the l=2 tidal forcing is in the gravity-wave traveling regime, with a one-way damping depth of \(8.9\times10^6\) and no discrete resonances, as long as the spin period exceeds about 45 min.
+- Dissipative. The static structural susceptibility is \(|\kappa_{\rm struct}|\le8.8\times10^{-9}\), which is \(2.2\times10^{-9}\) of \(|\beta|\).
+
+**Conjectural.** For J0337, a linear, passive, scalar-driven lag of the white-dwarf charge satisfies
+
+\begin{equation}
+|\delta\Delta|\le|\alpha_o||\kappa_{\rm lag}|\,\delta\varphi_{\rm mod},\qquad \delta\varphi_{\rm mod}\le3.08\times10^{-10}|\alpha_p|,
+\label{eq:wd-lag-bound}
+\end{equation}
+
+where the modulation comes from the inner eccentricity. With the Cassini limit \(|\alpha_o|\simeq|\alpha_0|\le3.5\times10^{-3}\) \cite{bertotti2003cassini}, reaching the stored two-day scale \(U=1.68\times10^{-9}\) of Section 5.3 requires \(|\kappa_{\rm lag}\alpha_p|\ge1.5\times10^3\). Even if all of \(|\beta|=4\) relaxed, the bound would be \(4.4\times10^{-12}|\alpha_p|\), and the free-fall mechanism gives \(7.5\times10^{-21}|\alpha_p|\). Within this linear scalar class, a lag at the Section 5 sensitivity must therefore reside in the neutron-star charge sector of Section 4.3.
+
+**Boundary statement.** This worked example is a no-go boundary, not a loophole. The minimal free-fall internal state exists at millisecond timescales as a transient scattering memory whose permanent value is zero, and at orbital timescales it collapses to static coefficients; assumption A4 holds for it. The remaining assumptions are:
+
+- positive damping of the radial modes;
+- neglect of interior Born scattering (core compactness about \(10^{-4}\));
+- the unfixed \(\varphi_\infty\) exponent of the \(10^{-8}\) direct part;
+- a non-gray correction that uses LTE continuum opacity only; non-LTE heating and line blanketing act in opposite directions;
+- a slowly rotating white dwarf;
+- a mixed hydrogen–helium envelope, whereas the observed star has a hydrogen (DA) atmosphere \cite{kaplan2014j0337}.
+
 ## 5. Conditional application to PSR J0337+1715
 
 ### 5.1 Data and template provenance
