+**Counterexample candidate.** Section 4.6 works through the smallest internal state of the white-dwarf carrier. At millisecond timescales its only memory is a transient retarded scattering signal with zero permanent charge. At orbital timescales it collapses to static coefficients in the radial, tidal and dissipative channels. A lag at the Section 5 sensitivity would therefore have to reside in the neutron-star charge sector of Section 4.3.
