317: ### 4.4 Physical-drive phases provide an additional gate
318: 
319: **Proven.** Let \(\boldsymbol r=\boldsymbol x_p-\boldsymbol x_i\), \(\boldsymbol R=\boldsymbol x_b-\boldsymbol x_o\), b be the inner center of mass, and \(f=m_i/(m_p+m_i)\). Then \(r_{po}=|\boldsymbol R+f\boldsymbol r|\). In the aligned coplanar limit, retain terms linear separately in eccentricity and \(f a_{\rm in}/a_{\rm out}\), dropping their products. With mean longitudes \(\lambda_p=n_{\rm in}(t-t_{{\rm asc},p})\), \(\lambda_b=n_{\rm out}(t-t_{{\rm asc},b})\), and \(M_A=\lambda_A-\varpi_A\),
